<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich von Gagern</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1880</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich von Gagern was a German liberal politician from the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. In March 1848 he became the grand duchy's chief minister, and in May he was elected president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt-parliament">Frankfurt National Assembly</a>, the first freely elected parliament for all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He later briefly led the Reich ministry and supported a German state under Prussian leadership without <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-gagern.jpg" alt="Heinrich von Gagern" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seib, Jacob · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seib,_Jacob_-_Portr%C3%A4t_Heinrich_von_Gagern_(Zeno_Fotografie).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
